.TH "ELEMENT.GETATTRIBUTENODENS" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Element.getAttributeNodeNS \- Element: getAttributeNodeNS() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]getAttributeNodeNS()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]Element\f[R] interface returns the specified namespaced attribute
of the specified element, as an \f[CR]Attr\f[R] node.
It returns \f[CR]null\f[R] if the element doesn\(cqt have an attribute
with the given name in the namespace.
.PP
This method is useful if you need the namespaced attribute\(cqs instance
properties.
If you only need the namespaced attribute\(cqs value, you can use the
\f[CR]getAttributeNS()\f[R] method instead.
.PP
If you are working with HTML documents and you don\(cqt need to specify
the requested attribute as being part of a specific namespace, use the
\f[CR]getAttributeNode()\f[R] method instead.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getAttributeNodeNS(namespace, localName)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]namespace\f[R]
A string specifying the namespace of the attribute, or \f[CR]null\f[R]
for no explicit namespace.
.TP
\f[B]localName\f[R]
A string specifying the name of the attribute.
.SS Return value
An \f[CR]Attr\f[R] node for the attribute, or \f[CR]null\f[R] if the
element doesn\(cqt have an attribute with the given name in the
namespace.
